        <div id="answer" data-section-target class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">The 30-second answer</h2>
          <div class="card">
            <p class="m-0">Make the session in charge a conductor that plans, delegates, merges and reports, and never writes product code. Write each piece of work as a unit contract that names the files it owns and the evidence that proves it done. Send every finished unit to a fresh verifier and every finding to a refuter. Merge one unit at a time through a lock, with the gate run on the staged merge. Let a watcher deploy main every 10 minutes, smoke every sitemap URL and roll back on a failure. Then turn each break into a script, a gate or a role before the next unit starts.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-6">The templates come from two builds that ran on one Mac in October 2026. Rightmark helps companies license private data to AI developers. Dylan is an AI SDR that books B2B meetings and bills when they are held. Each template is rewritten from the real file, opens with the break it prevents, and says what to change first. Start with the conductor prompt, the unit contract and the two scripts.</p>
        </div>

