                <text x="419.2" y="356.0" style="fill:rgb(var(--muted, 170 167 154))" font-size="14" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">pages</text>
                <text x="20.0" y="386.0" style="fill:rgb(var(--muted, 170 167 154))" font-size="14" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">Source: the Dylan build program log; the live</text>
                <text x="20.0" y="405.0" style="fill:rgb(var(--muted, 170 167 154))" font-size="14" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">sitemap counted 12 October 2026.</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
          </figure>
          <p>Add one end-to-end on production after each deploy. Dylan's waitlist answered 503 on every step after the first, because the blob store served a weak etag the update check never matched; local tests used a file store. And deploy the commit yourself: Dylan's host never deployed the Phase 3 merge, and the conductor had to deploy that exact commit through the API.</p>
          <CopyBlock client:visible text={TEMPLATE_WATCHER} filename="scripts/deploy-watcher.sh" language="bash" />
        </div>

        <div id="guard" data-section-target class="scroll-mt-24 mt-14">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">8. The guard hook and the content lint</h2>
          <p>Dylan's kit shipped two hooks. One blocks shell commands that push to main, force push, skip checks, deploy to production, write DNS, switch payments to live, read secrets, put dashes in commits or edit the guardrails. The other blocks file writes that add dashes or secrets or touch the guardrails, and refuses to read env files. The first hook's header calls it "a seatbelt, not a security boundary". On install, five probe payloads were refused: echo a secret, push to main, write a dash, read an env file and an unscoped CLI call.</p>
          <p>Rightmark's content firewall scans every commit for names and phrases that must never ship, and on day one a probe showed it missed two banned phrases and the names of public AI labs. So this template probes every banned phrase, and its self-test fails if any of them gets through.</p>
          <CopyBlock client:visible text={TEMPLATE_GUARD} filename=".claude/hooks/guard-hook.mjs" language="js" />
        </div>

        <div id="budget" data-section-target class="scroll-mt-24 mt-14">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">9. The budget card</h2>
          <p>On 11 October the parallel slots across Rightmark's runs summed to 11, the Mac's load hit 460 and gates timed out. The same day a test leak filled the disk and a stale 906 MB build folder held the merge lock for more than 80 minutes. On the Dylan platform build the load reached about 900 and the Docker daemon died.</p>
          <p>The rules that came out: about 5 units in flight per machine, a disk floor, CI as the gate, and a stop at 1.5 times any estimate. Dylan's Phase 0 hit that line: 21.8M tokens against an estimate of 12M, 1.82 times, because it wrote 14 decision records instead of 10, ran 126 agents instead of about 100, and its writers and judges read more than planned. Its Phase 2 and Phase 4 token totals were never recorded, so only the estimates exist: 6M to 8M and 10M to 14M. The 5-hour usage window is a planning input: write its reset time in the status file.</p>
