        <div id="taste" data-section-target class="scroll-mt-24 mt-14">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">10. The taste lock</h2>
          <p>On 8 October rightmark.ai went live, and the same day I sent the homepage back: "its not the website we initially design". The swarm's own style rules had rewritten copy from the design I approved on 4 October, a 56-page prototype built by five parallel builders. The fix was a rule that makes that design binding, 15 parity units that brought it back, and parity as a check in the full gate.</p>
          <p>Taste does not delegate. Write down what is approved, make it a reference the gate can compare against, and list every forced difference with the rule that forced it.</p>
          <CopyBlock client:visible text={TEMPLATE_TASTE} filename="taste-lock.md" language="markdown" />
        </div>

        <div class="card mt-14">
          <p class="mt-0">Repo Check is the free local script that values a Git repo on your own machine; it also runs as a Claude skill. <a href="https://rightmark.ai/repo-check/">https://rightmark.ai/repo-check/</a></p>
          <p>Dylan is an AI SDR billed per held meeting. Join the waitlist: <a href="https://meetdylan.ai/waitlist">https://meetdylan.ai/waitlist</a></p>
          <p class="mb-0 text-sm" style="color: rgb(var(--muted))">How the two builds ran, failure by failure: <a href={`${base}/chapters/58-conductor-never-codes/`}>Chapter 58: The Conductor Never Codes</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div id="do-this" data-section-target class="scroll-mt-24 mt-14">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">Do this Monday</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>Paste the conductor prompt into a fresh session on a repo you know, fill in the ask-first list, and give it one small feature.</li>
            <li>Have it write three units in the contract format, with no file owned twice, and send one through a fresh verifier and a refuter.</li>
            <li>Install merge-unit.sh, set GATE_CMD to your quick gate, run <code>bash scripts/merge-unit.sh compose</code> on all three unit branches in one throwaway tree, then merge them one at a time through the lock.</li>
            <li>Run <code>bash scripts/deploy-watcher.sh --once</code> against staging on a good commit, then break one page, run it again and watch it roll back. Only then point it at production.</li>
            <li>Install the guard hook, run --self-test, add one banned phrase of your own and run it again. Fill in the budget card before the next run.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-6 text-sm" style="color: rgb(var(--muted))">Related: <a href={`${base}/chapters/58-conductor-never-codes/`}>Ch 58: The Conductor Never Codes</a> · <a href={`${base}/chapters/06-the-swarm/`}>Ch 06: Parallel Subagents and Fan-Out</a> · <a href={`${base}/chapters/28-failure-receipts/`}>Ch 28: Six Failures, Six Bills</a> · <a href={`${base}/chapters/38-run-until-done/`}>Ch 38: Run Until Done</a> · <a href={`${base}/chapters/53-first-real-caller/`}>Ch 53: The First Real Caller</a> · <a href={`${base}/swarms/`}>Swarms</a> · <a href={`${base}/dynamic-workflows/`}>Dynamic workflows</a> · <a href={`${base}/agent-workflow/`}>Agent workflow</a></p>
        </div>

